WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.280
New Guinea looks like another planet.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.110
In fact, it looks like it belongs in J.R.R.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.510
Tolkien’s Middle Earth.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:16.880
But if this were the case, it would definitely
be Mordor.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:25.310
A place where things like this are happening
right now, in the 21st century...

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:28.720
Missing explorer discovered in Papua New Guinea
Benedict Allen disappeared while searching

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.480
for a remote tribe in the South Pacific nation
And I know what you are going to say...

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:31.480
Come on Simon!

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.720
One bad story doesn’t mean the whole island
is that bad!

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.230
Yes, you’re right.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:41.670
It’s even worse.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:45.680
Papua New Guinea: Women and children killed
in tribal massacre

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:46.680
And now you might be wondering...

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:50.039
Why on earth are we talking to you about New
Guinea today on VisualPolitik?

00:00:50.039 --> 00:00:53.210
What kind of political issues can they have
going on?

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:56.430
But believe me, there is a lot to talk about
here.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:03.149
First of all, New Guinea is the third biggest
island on the planet, after Australia and

00:01:03.149 --> 00:01:04.149
Greenland.

00:01:04.149 --> 00:01:06.110
But there is something more.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:10.690
If you pay attention to the map, you can see
the island is divided into two halves by a

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:12.190
perfectly straight line.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:16.820
This is the border that separates PAPUA NEW
GUINEA, a sovereign state, from WESTERN PAPUA,

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.439
a region of Indonesia.

00:01:18.439 --> 00:01:22.520
It is here, in the Indonesian part, where
a big separatist movement has emerged.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:26.280
So...what would be at stake if Papua became
independent from Indonesia?

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:32.409
Well, right here you have one very good reason.

00:01:32.409 --> 00:01:38.430
Freeport’s Gold Mine in Papua Largest in
the World

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:39.430
Exactly!

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:43.260
We’re talking about gold, copper and, yes,
oil and gas.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.829
Remember when I compared Papua to Mordor?

00:01:45.829 --> 00:01:51.829
Well Papua even has its own Mount Doom where
you can make gold rings and many other things.

00:01:51.829 --> 00:01:56.450
This explains why Papuan nationalism is a
headache for many.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:00.369
So today’s question is, what do Papuans
really want from Indonesia?

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:05.479
Do they want to be their own country or would
they rather join their Eastern neighbours?

00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:07.590
Can they get the sovereignty they want?

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:12.100
Today we are going to answer all of these
questions but, before we do, let’s look

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:17.040
back at the history of this island.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:24.100
THE ISLAND NOBODY CARED ABOUT
Over the years, New Guinea was controlled

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:26.680
by the United Kingdom, Germany and the Netherlands.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:31.440
And I say “controlled” because New Guinea
was considered so worthless that nobody was

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.580
interested in turning it into a proper colony.

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:37.580
Each of these European powers just planted
a flag and created a harbor so they could

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.270
control the sea routes surrounding the island.

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:44.160
But nobody really cared about what was going
on on the island itself.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:48.489
So, most of the indigenous people of New Guinea
didn’t even realize they had been conquered

00:02:48.489 --> 00:02:49.970
or colonized by anybody.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:54.629
So, of course, they kept their tribal system
the same as it had been before.

00:02:54.629 --> 00:02:58.680
This also explains why nobody really tried
to take control of New Guinea during the period

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.250
of decolonization.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:08.849
Basically, during the 1960s and 70s, all the
European powers left the island and divided

00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:09.849
it into two parts.

00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:13.319
The line that divides New Guinea is the 141st
meridian.

00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:17.879
From this line to the East is Papua New Guinea,
an independent, sovereign country.

00:03:17.879 --> 00:03:21.370
From this line to the West, we have an Indonesian
province.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:25.040
And you might be wondering... what were all
those tribes doing while all this was happening?

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:29.590
So, as I said earlier... many of them had
no idea about any of these political maneuvers.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:33.010
Most of them didn’t even see European people
in their day-to-day lives.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:36.319
For example, the DANI is one of the biggest
Papuan ethnicities.

00:03:36.319 --> 00:03:43.349
They had been living a Stone Age existence
until 1938, when a plane flew over the Great

00:03:43.349 --> 00:03:44.409
Dani Valley.

00:03:44.409 --> 00:03:50.230
This was the first contact this tribe had
had with people from outside the tribe.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:56.180
And this is far from a minority group.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:04:01.510
Dani tribes are estimated to have more than
200,000 people and they represent around 5%

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:03.920
of the Indonesian Papuan population.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:08.629
Yes, technically they are Indonesian but many
of them are not even aware of this.

00:04:08.629 --> 00:04:15.129
And you might think that by now, 2019, things
have changed: civilization and internet connections

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:16.769
are everywhere, right?

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:17.860
Absolutely not!

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:24.260
Just look at this news story...

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:29.860
This remote tribe in New Guinea cuts boys’
skin with razors so they look like crocodiles

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:35.010
And yes, I said tribes, in plural, because
on this island there are more than 1000 tribes.

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:38.570
And perhaps there are many more that we don’t
even know about.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:39.670
And you might say...

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.970
Why did Indonesia take the Western part?

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:44.970
The answer is that Indonesia was formerly
a Dutch colony.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:48.910
So, when they got their independence, they
claimed this Dutch controlled territory too.

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:53.250
Since none of these tribes protested, it was
given to the brand new Indonesian state.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:56.830
And Indonesians quickly learned to care about
this worthless island.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:05:00.730
Basically, since the moment SUHARTO, the Indonesian
dictator and father of the nation, first set

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:04.790
foot on this island, he realized there was
much more there than crazy tribal people.

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:09.030
Today, one third of the gas that Indonesia
exports is produced in Papua.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:13.280
And then, we have the GRASBERG mine.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:16.230
Wow!!!

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:22.790
Everyday Freeport Produces 240 kg of Gold
from Papua!

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:25.090
But wait a minute because it doesn’t end
there.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:30.070
This Grasberg mine is not only the World’s
largest gold mine; it is also the second largest

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:31.070
when it comes to copper.

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:35.340
Yes, dear viewers of VisualPolitik, Papua
gives a lot in exchange for not very much

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:36.790
from the Indonesians.

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:40.030
And this explains why Indonesia is not willing
to let them go.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:44.490
In fact, the current Indonesian president,
JOKO WIDODO is going in the opposite direction.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:48.900
Yes, until recently the Grasberg mine was
owned by a private company and Indonesia has

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:55.930
just nationalized it.

00:05:55.930 --> 00:06:01.410
Indonesia Wrests Control of Freeport’s Grasberg
Mine, Ending Long Battle

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:06.110
But make no mistake, Indonesian interest for
Papua New Guinea ends with the island’s

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:07.110
resources.

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:10.630
Papuan citizens are considered second class
citizens and the Indonesians look at them

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:11.630
as inferior.

00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:14.770
Racism is so blatant that they are usually
called ‘the monkeys’.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:18.100
And yes, to most of the Papuans, this is an
insult...

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:23.810
Papuans turn monkey slur into a revolutionary
symbol

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:27.670
These days, with the government lead by Joko
WIDODO, things are changing, though.

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:31.311
The Indonesian government is starting to build
some highways and passing some laws that are

00:06:31.311 --> 00:06:32.780
more friendly to the indigenous people.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:35.350
But none of this is enough for the Papuan
nationalists.

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:37.380
And now you might be wondering...

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:39.770
So what do the Indonesian Papuans really want?

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:42.850
Do they want to join their Eastern neighbours?

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:46.290
Let’s take a look.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:48.020
BAD PAPUA AND...

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:51.500
EVEN WORSE PAPUA
Life is hard in Indonesian Papua... but it

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:54.870
is heaven compared with life in Independent
Papua.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:58.050
Basically, if a tribe gets you there, you
could become their dinner.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.540
And no, I am not exaggerating.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:06.940
Couple kidnapped by CANNIBALS and tortured
on dream holiday to Papua New Guinea

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:09.570
But wait a minute because the cities are not
much better!

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:12.990
Port Moresby, the capital, is considered the
World’s most dangerous city.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:15.900
It is controlled by the RASKOL, the local
street gangs.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:18.270
Their hobbies include alcohol, drugs and killing.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:20.120
And I know what you are thinking...

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:21.120
Come on Simon!

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.390
There are lots of dangerous cities in the
world!

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:25.390
Are you sure Port Moresby is that exceptional?

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:26.910
Well, yes!

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:29.100
Look what happened during the APEC summit.

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:32.790
The APEC summit is the Asia Pacific Economic
Cooperation forum.

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:42.690
In 2018 they wanted to hold a meeting here
and... this is what happened.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:46.060
Papua New Guinea hosts APEC CEO Summit on
cruise ship

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:50.240
Yes, no matter how many security companies
and bodyguards they could hire, politicians

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.690
said they would not set foot on land there.

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:56.430
So the whole event had to be held on a cruise
ship, docked next to the coast.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:08:00.280
Extreme poverty rates in Papua New Guinea
are as high as 40%.

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:03.360
In comparison, the rate in neighbouring Indonesian
Papua is 25%.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:06.580
While elsewhere in Indonesia the rate drops
to around 6%.

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:11.050
Of course, we should take all these statistics
with a pinch of salt because, as you can imagine,

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:17.400
there are many areas on this island where
nobody can really collect reliable data.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:25.211
Anyway, Indonesian papuans don’t want their
gas, oil and gold to be stolen by the Indonesians.

00:08:25.211 --> 00:08:28.430
But they don’t want them to be stolen by
their Eastern neighbors either.

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:30.760
Basically, they want it all for themselves.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:34.300
BENNY WENDA is a separatist leader who lives
in exile in London.

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:37.080
His goal is to rule what he hopes to name
WESTERN PAPUA.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:40.830
But the question is... could this territory
really become independent?

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:46.030
You see, the Western Papua Liberation Movement,
led by Benny Wenda, has collected 1.8 million

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:49.450
signatures to request the United Nations hold
a referendum.

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:52.890
Now let’s see what could happen if they
really go through with this referendum.

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:54.070
How might it play out?

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:59.440
Let’s step back in time for a moment!

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:04.640
THE NOKEN SYSTEM
We said that nobody really protested when

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.330
Western Papua fell into Indonesian hands.

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:09.080
Well... this is not exactly true.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:14.600
As we told you earlier, Indonesian Papua was
controlled by the Netherlands.

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:21.010
After World War II, Indonesia became independent
and wanted to have Papua as part of their

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:22.010
territory.

00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:23.860
But the Dutch said this made no sense.

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:24.860
Think about it.

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:28.060
There are more than 3,500 kilometers between
Jakarta and Papua.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:31.420
They don’t have any economic, historical
or cultural links.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:36.140
So, in order to solve this problem they decided
to hold a referendum.

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:37.140
The problem?

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:40.050
Well... good luck trying to have free, fair
and transparent elections in a place with

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:41.500
1000 tribes.

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:49.660
The 1969 referendum, also known as the Free
Election Act, was a charade.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:55.022
Theoretically, 800,000 papuans were eligible
to vote.

00:09:55.022 --> 00:10:01.780
But only 1000 people, selected by the Indonesian
army, ended up voting and they did it by...

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:02.780
raising their hand!

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:06.510
What’s more, troops made sure that there
was just one option to choose from.

00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:11.590
So, of course, the result of the referendum
was a unanimous cry to become part of Indonesia!

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:12.590
But I know what you are thinking.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:15.240
Back then, Indonesia was under the dictatorship
of SUKARNO.

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:18.780
You cannot expect a dictator to organize free
and fair elections.

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:20.060
But now things are different.

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:23.950
Indonesia is a democracy and that should be
true for Papua as well.

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:25.970
Nevertheless, the problem is still the same...

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:28.270
How can you organize elections in such a tribal
country?

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:33.120
Here is where the NOKEN system comes into
the picture!

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:38.250
NOKEN means, in some Papuan dialects, BAG.

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:42.630
Basically, the tribal chiefs go to the electoral
body with a bag full of votes and they say

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:44.290
‘this is what my people voted’.

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:46.110
In some cases, there is not even a bag.

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:48.740
The electoral body just go to the tribal chief
and ask directly.

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:51.440
--So who are you going to vote for in the
next elections?

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:55.380
--Bfff I’ve got no idea, man... maybe...
the X party.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:59.560
Yes, I will vote for that one, the one with
the green logo.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:00.560
--Aha!

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:06.160
Very good! and... how many people do you have
in your tribe?

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:07.160
--People?

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:09.200
I have no idea, man!

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.200
ehm...

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:14.020
I guess around 300 hundred people... and well,
35 goats.

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:19.520
Because, you know, in our tribe, we believe
goats count as humans so I guess they would

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:21.070
get a vote too, right?

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:23.660
--Aha... so that works out to three... hundred...
and thirty five votes for the X party...

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:24.660
So very good, sir!

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:25.660
Thank you for voting and have a nice day!

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:28.430
As you can imagine, with such a well-organized
system, it is no surprise that the current

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:34.310
Indonesian president, JOKO WIDODO, won a landslide
victory in New Guinea by having even more

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:44.590
votes than voters!

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:49.400
Papuan Electoral College finds more than one
million people who voted twice in the 2019

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.580
elections
Now imagine what would happen with this system

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:53.190
on a self-determination referendum.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:58.630
It would be easy for Papuan independentists
to claim all the tribes voted for self determination.

00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:03.860
Also, don’t forget that one third of the
population resident in Papua comes from Indonesia.

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:09.180
And this is, in fact, the third of the population
that can be easily counted on a census.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:13.830
In other words: the outcome of this referendum
would largely depend on who gets to organize

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:14.830
it.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:17.110
And besides, most of the Papuans wouldn’t
even care!

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:22.240
Perhaps, they still don’t even know that
they are considered Indonesians now!

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:25.760
So this is why the question is now over to
you...

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:29.620
Can Western Papua get out of poverty and become
an independent state?

00:12:29.620 --> 00:12:34.050
Do you think they can ever get past tribalism...
or would it be better to let them be?

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:36.420
Please, leave your answer in the comment section
below.

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:40.680
Also don’t forget to visit our friends from
RECONSIDER MEDIA.COM, the podcast that provided

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:42.930
the vocals on this episode that were not mine.

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:44.980
If you like this video, give us a thumbs up.

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:57.420
And, as always, I’ll see you next time.

